# Surfaces where an accidental change is expensive and a review is cheap.
#
# These are review requirements, not authorship restrictions: anyone may
# propose a change to any of them. Paired with the "require review from Code
# Owners" branch protection setting on main, an owner has to look before it
# lands.
#
# Each entry covers itself. This file is under /.github/, and the rulesync
# sources own the generated agent trees, so relaxing a rule needs the same
# review as the change the rule was there to catch. A control that a single
# commit can remove alongside the thing it guards is not a control.

# Workflows, actions, and this file. A workflow change can widen the
# deployment job's privileges or stop the merge gate from gating, and both
# read as ordinary diffs.
/.github/ @wfscot

# The gates themselves: lint, locked-SDD, and rulesync generation. A change
# here changes what every other change is checked against.
/scripts/ @wfscot

# Policy that agents load as instructions. The generated trees are projections
# of these sources, so owning the sources owns what every session is told.
/.rulesync/ @wfscot
